# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads as the build context.
#
# This file exists to STOP gcloud falling back to .gitignore, which it does when
# no .gcloudignore is present. That fallback is a footgun for a Docker build:
# generated-but-required files are gitignored by definition, so the daemon sees
# a context subtly different from any developer's disk. It cost us one build
# (next-env.d.ts, free-beta D3) before this file existed.
#
# Keep in sync with .dockerignore. Everything here must be either regenerated by
# the build or genuinely unnecessary — when in doubt, leave it out of this file
# and let .dockerignore make the call, since that one is evaluated against a
# context we can actually inspect.

.git
.gitignore
node_modules
.next
out
coverage

# Secrets: the context is uploaded to a GCS bucket. Never relax these two.
.env*
!.env.example

.claude
docs
backups
.vercel
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
*.pem
